        When you search Google for a word counter, 99% of top-ranking utilities require uploading your file to their remote backend server. The file is stored in temporary buckets (or cached indefinitely on third-party servers), processed by an unknown server-side script, and deleted after hours or days.
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
        For everyday publicly available documents, this may be acceptable. However, for professionals handling proprietary information, cloud uploads represent a serious security hazard:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
